PATENT-CHAIN INTERPRETATION: raw Eq. 21 data, the source's
unconditioned Figure 0.5 choices, and Eq. 24's pseudoinverse.
NOT LITERAL EQ. 22: the rendered source prints an undefined
2*pi*t factor and mutually inconsistent matrix dimensions;
this code uses the conventional exp(j*Kz*z), k-by-F form.

CAVEAT: in Eqs. 21-24 the tomographic baseline is formed from
along-orbit sub-aperture phase-centre separations. An along-track
separation is not an elevation baseline. Whether such a geometry
carries depth information is the method's principal open question.
The depth axis above is scaled by the ASSUMED velocity and frequency
recorded here, neither of which is measured by this software. Do not
present these depths as measurements without the null test and the
parameter-sensitivity sweep alongside.
